    "created_at": "2021-02-10T16:31:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-02-10T16:31:22Z",
    "body": "The Console specification deliberately under specifies what implementations do with calls to most API methods, to allow implementations large flexibility in surfacing this information to developers (eg, in a GUI, terminal messages, web page viewing the status of a remote agent, etc).\r\n\r\nAgents are already free to define hooks and be compliant with this specification. Is there a need for such functionality to be defined here?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
